# Archcheck binary (built locally by scripts/archcheck/).
# Anchored with leading '/' so the pattern matches only the root-level
# build artifact. Without the anchor, gitignore treats `archcheck` as
# matching any PATH COMPONENT named that way, which recursively excludes
# the entire `scripts/archcheck/` tree (the W1 PR1 regression surfaced this).
/archcheck

# Docker secrets (never commit tokens)
secrets/

# PR1 (Repository truth, June 2026):
#   * scripts/archcheck/current_report.json is a per-run diagnostic snapshot
#     of the codebase scan; regenerated cheaply on every `go run ./scripts/archcheck`.
#   * It is NEVER used as an allowlist (see docs/migrations/api-infrastructure-imports-allowlist.txt
#     for the single source of truth on the ratchet).
#   * Keeping it out-of-tree avoids polluting PR diffs with full-repo snapshots.
scripts/archcheck/current_report.json
# Validation transient logs (NOT shipped):
ci_output.txt
ci_full_output.txt
/tmp/build.out
/tmp/vet.out
/tmp/test.out

# ci/archcheck-hard-fail: E2E sentinel marker for scripts/ci-archcheck-e2e.sh.
# The file is created + deleted by the E2E harness; if a run aborts
# mid-step (SIGINT, OOM, runner network drop) the sentinel is left
# orphaned on disk. gitignore it so subsequent CI + local pre-commit
# runs do not see it as an unintended violation.
internal/api/_dummy_archcheck_regression.go

# Wave staging artefacts: temp splice blocks + python runners used by an
# operator-only pipeline (e.g. `.wave23_piper.py`) to register a wave
# entry on origin/main. The artefacts are single-use per wave and SHOULD
# NOT be committed — `.wave23_*` glob catches the canonical pre-commit
# state. Was leak-prone in June 2026 when these landed in the working
# tree between the fast-forward and the conditional cleanup; this entry
# closes the gap (housekeeping precondition for the next wave).
.wave23_*
# Scratch quarantine - never-tracked prior in-progress work (P0.4 / P0.3 voiceover scratch)
# Moved 2026-06-29 as part of P0.6 closure so canonical main stays build-clean.
docs/notes/scratch/

# PR-A (June 2026): anti-reintro gate for diagnostic / snapshot artefacts
# that historically leaked into the working tree during mega-batch
# commits (the paste audit `tmp-diag` family). Patterns are
# subdir-safe via the trailing `/` (anchored to root) and case-sensitive
# (matches the rg-dir basename, NOT a substring of a longer name like
# `make-tmp-diag.sh`). CI enforcement lives in
# scripts/ci-architectural-checks.sh::Check 36 (forward-prevention gate,
# mirrors Check 5 / Check 8 alignment).
.tmp-diag/
tmp-diag/
CURRENT_*.go
TODO[0-9]*.go

# TTS-cleaned voiceover artifacts (regenerated from lyrics pipeline)
/cleaned_*.mp3
/cleaned_*.wav
/cleaned_*.ogg
